```
Title: AWS Bucket Block Public Access Weakened
Author: Shoban Chiddarth
Date: 2026-10-21
Level: medium
Description: Detects the weakening of "Block Public Access" setting of S3 buckets in CloudTrail logs.
 Monitoring changes to Block Public Access settings is critical, as attackers may disable these safeguards before exposing a bucket through a public ACL or bucket policy.
MITRE Tactic: Uncategorized
Tags: attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1686.001
Reference: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/cloud/aws/cloudtrail/aws_cloudtrail_bucket_block_public_access_weakened.yml
 False Positives:
   - Administrators intentionally modifying Block Public Access settings to support a legitimate application or public bucket configuration.
```
eventName="PutBucketPublicAccessBlock" eventSource="s3.amazonaws.com" requestParameters.PublicAccessBlockConfiguration.BlockPublicAcls="false" OR requestParameters.PublicAccessBlockConfiguration.BlockPublicPolicy="false" OR requestParameters.PublicAccessBlockConfiguration.IgnorePublicAcls="false" OR requestParameters.PublicAccessBlockConfiguration.RestrictPublicBuckets="false" NOT errorCode=* OR errorCode="Success"